\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 The High Elvis\'92 office was more like a TV set, with a dais, a semicircle of chairs arranged like a tribunal, and a wall display that could probably show the weather in heaven if you paid for the lux subscription. There was also a bar and a sandwich frying station, and the smell of lard was thickening the air. The High Elvis\'92 stood in front of the dais, in full regalia and fully exhausted. There were dark smudges under his eyes, and his cape hung like it was heavy with bad news. Behind him, a row of cabinet Elvi hovered, dimmed, like a strip of Vegas signage with half the bulbs blown.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

